{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Music Generation \u2014 MusicGen, Stable Audio, Suno, and the Licensing Earthquake Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: generate with MusicGen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from audiocraft.models import MusicGen"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torchaudio"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model = MusicGen.get_pretrained(\"facebook/musicgen-small\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "model.set_generation_params(duration=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wav = model.generate([\"upbeat synthwave with driving drums, 128 BPM\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "torchaudio.save(\"out.wav\", wav[0].cpu(), 32000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three sizes: `small` (300M, fast), `medium` (1.5B), `large` (3.3B). Small is enough for \"does the idea land.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: melody conditioning"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "melody, sr = torchaudio.load(\"humming.wav\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "wav = model.generate_with_chroma("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    [\"jazz piano cover\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    melody.squeeze(),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sr,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "MusicGen-melody takes a chromagram and preserves the tune while swapping timbre. Useful for \"give me this melody as a string quartet.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: FAD evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from frechet_audio_distance import FrechetAudioDistance"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "fad = FrechetAudioDistance()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "fad.get_fad_score(\"generated_folder/\", \"reference_folder/\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Computes VGGish-embedding distance. Useful for genre-level regression tests; not a substitute for human listeners."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: adding to the LLM-music workflow"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Combine with the ideas from Lessons 7-8:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "prompt = \"Write a 30-second jazz loop. Describe the drums, bass, and piano voicing.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "description = llm.complete(prompt)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "music = musicgen.generate([description], duration=30)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Run `code/main.py`. It produces a \"generative\" chord progression + drum pattern as ASCII symbols \u2014 a music-gen cartoon. Play it back via any MIDI renderer if you want.\n2. **Medium.** Install `audiocraft`, generate 10-second clips across 4 genre prompts with MusicGen-small, measure FAD against a reference genre set.\n3. **Hard.** Using ACE-Step (or MusicGen-melody), generate three variations of the same tune with different timbre prompts. Compute CLAP similarity to the prompt to verify alignment."
      ]
    }
